# CPU name rules: the noise removed from the CPU name on every OS.
#
# match|action|pattern|text
#
# Same format as hw/gpu.db (see there for the actions). 'match' is '*' for
# rules that apply to every CPU.
#
# './neofetch-edit try cpu "<name>"' shows what a name turns into.

*|del|(TM)|
*|del|(tm)|
*|del|(R)|
*|del|(r)|
*|del|CPU|
*|del|Processor|
*|del|Dual-Core|
*|del|Quad-Core|
*|del|Six-Core|
*|del|Eight-Core|
*|del|[1-9][0-9]-Core|
*|del|[0-9]-Core|
*|del|, * Compute Cores|

# Intel: 'Core i7-6500U' is shown as 'i7-6500U', but the newer names
# ('Core Ultra 7 155H', 'Core 7 150U') make no sense without 'Core'.
*Intel*|del|[0-9][0-9]th Gen |
*Intel*|keep|Core Ultra |
*Intel*|keep|Core [3579] |
*|del|Core |

*|del|("AuthenticAMD"*)|
*|del|with Radeon*|
*|del|w/ Radeon*|
*|del|, altivec supported|
*|del|FPU*|
*|del|Chip Revision*|
*|del|Technologies, Inc|
*|sub|Core2|Core 2
